@template earnest
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- I think that's yesterday's shirt? Sorry. Just saying.
- I wore mine twice once. Nobody minded. Much.   #funny
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- If you're short of clean ones, the laundry's easy. Honest.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- Oh, you've got grime on you. Quite a lot, actually.
- Hard job? It looks like a hard job. On your sleeves.   #funny
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- You should change. Not that you look bad. Just oily.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- Oh, hello! I'm glad it's you. Really.
- {hi}! How are you? Properly, I mean.
- {hi}, {nick}. I was hoping I'd see you today.
- Hello! Sorry, was I in the way? I think I was.
- {hi}. Can I ask you something? Later, maybe.
- {hi}! I'm doing my best today. You?
- Oh, hi. I've been meaning to say hello. Hello.
- {hi}. I learned something new today. Two things.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}! You're one of the people I trust here.
- {hi}. Thanks for last time. I don't think I said.
? time:morning
- Good morning! I'm trying to be a morning person.
? time:evening
- Evening! Did today go well for you? I hope so.
== near
- I'm trying to get this right. Is it right? I think so.
- {room}. I've nearly got the hang of this place.
- Sorry, one second. I don't want to lose my place.
- I'm being careful. Being careful takes ages.
- Can you watch? Tell me if I do it wrong.
- I've done this three times. Fourth time's lucky.
- It's harder than it looks. Everything is.
- Almost done! Then I can talk properly.
